# Credentials. .env.example is the template; the real one never leaves the machine.
# Every spelling, not just `.env` -- a `.env.local-backup` holding the same key
# sat untracked beside it, one `git add -A` away from being committed.
.env*
!.env.example

# The virtualenv (550 MB) and everything that rebuilds from uv.lock.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Scratch: SWE-bench checkouts the SDK workspace makes, and its own event store.
# Regenerated on every run, ~100 MB.
.cache/

# Instance images kept as gzipped `docker save`, so each is pulled from the registry
# once ever. ~1 GB each, ~15 GB for the set -- data, and reproducible from the registry
# given hours. See openhands_f2p/image_cache.py; F2P_IMAGE_CACHE moves it.
image-cache/
image-cache-evaluation/

# The SWE-bench Verified dump, 8 MB of someone else's data and a download rather
# than a source file. See openhands_f2p/dataset.py for how to fetch it.
data/

# Raw prompt and response bytes, one file per model call, written on every run. The
# least-read artefact in a run directory by a wide margin -- the trajectory, the flow log
# and the tool log carry the same events in a form people actually open. 143 MB across the
# four evaluation runs alone.
#
# Matched at any depth, under any parent. This has been narrowed twice by accident:
# `out/*/completions/` stopped applying the moment a series wrote to its own root, and
# `out*/**/completions/` stopped applying the moment a run lived somewhere not starting
# with "out" -- which is how 1319 evaluation completions reached a commit.
**/completions/
# ...except the judge's: one call per YES run, and nothing else records what the judge was
# asked and answered word for word (the agent's are summarised in trajectory.json).
!**/judge/completions/

.DS_Store
.ruff_cache/

# Validation and smoke runs of out-v2 experiments: scratch, named with a leading underscore.
swe-bench-outs/out-v2/_*/
swe-bench-outs/out-v2/__pycache__/
# Build and launch logs of dataset runs.
*-outs/_logs/
datasets/*/instances.lock
